# Pairs with DecisionDurability, and reaches the half of it the flip mutation
# does not: the unset. The cleanup retires the registry row without waiting for
# every participant to apply its terminal, which is the precondition
# ITxRegistryGrain.ForgetAsync states for itself. Unlike DecisionFlip this
# perturbs a protocol action rather than adding one, so it shows the third
# conjunct constrains the modelled protocol, not merely that it is well-formed.
MODULE: DecisionDurabilityEarlyForget
TARGET: DecisionDurability
CLASS: Action
SUMMARY: retires the registry row before every participant has applied its terminal
PERTURBS: ForgetDecision

--- FIND
    /\ \A k \in Written(t) : terminal[t][k] # "none"
    /\ \A k \in Written(t) : pend[t][k] = "none"
    /\ forgotten' = [forgotten EXCEPT ![t] = TRUE]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the drain-before-cleanup ordering is dropped.
    /\ forgotten' = [forgotten EXCEPT ![t] = TRUE]
--- END
